🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- element STRIDE of a `lit`-alias array field
🚽 matches its C layout, not sizeof(int). A `chungus` (union) overlays a
🚽 `Big vals[2]` (thicc = long long, 8-byte elements) with a `yap b[16]`
🚽 byte view. Writing vals[0]=1, vals[1]=2 must put vals[1] at byte 8
🚽 (b[8]), giving "1 0 2 0" -- a 4-byte stride would give "1 2 0 0" (PR
🚽 #256 review). long long is 8 bytes on both LP64 and wasm32, so this is
🚽 platform-independent.
lit thicc rizz Big;

chungus Overlay {
    Big vals[2];
    yap b[16];
};

skibidi main {
    chungus Overlay o;
    o.vals[0] = 1;
    o.vals[1] = 2;
    yapping("%d %d %d %d", o.b[0], o.b[4], o.b[8], o.b[12]);
}
